/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-33-
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-34-  // float % float (e.g. `number % 1.0` = the fractional part). OPAQUE for kprove, concrete for
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-35-  // krun. Python's float `%` is floor-based: a % b = a - floor(a/b)*b (K's %Float is IEEE
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-36-  // remainder, which differs — 3.5 %Float 1.0 = -0.5 vs Python 0.5 — so it is NOT used).
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-37-  syntax Float ::= floatMod(Float, Float) [function, total, symbol(floatMod), no-evaluators]
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-38-  rule floatMod(F1:Float, F2:Float) => F1 -Float (floorFloat(F1 /Float F2) *Float F2) [concrete]
