/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-1-// reference/src/semantics/call.k — MPY-CALL
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-2-// ONE call route for every callable: evaluate the callee to a VALUE (name lookup reaches
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-3-// builtins at the root; a cooled Attribute is a bound method), evaluate the args (the shared
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:4:// #evalArgs loop in core.k), then dispatch on the callee value:
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:5://   closureVal    -> bind params, push a frame (user function)
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-6-//   boundMethodV  -> applyMethod
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:7://   builtinV      -> the #iterNext folds (sum/all/any/max/min) or applyBuiltin
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-8-//   typeV         -> callable type objects: int(...) / str(...)
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-9-
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-10-module MPY-CALL
--
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-17-
/reference/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-18-  // evaluate callee, then args ([owise]: problem-local Call interceptions beat this)
